    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll**, who stands as our clear top play with a 75.69 efficiency score. His matchup against Gausman is balanced by the massive boost we get from Gausman\u2019s slow delivery to the plate, which creates an elite environment for **Corbin Carroll** to secure the stolen bases that remain our highest priority. **Seiya Suzuki** follows close behind at 71.14; he benefits significantly from facing Kelly, whose 5.27 xERA is the most exploitable arm on the board today. While **Gabriel Moreno** also draws Gausman, his #3 spot in the order provides enough stability to keep him in the starting slots despite the tougher matchup.\n\nWe are leaning heavily into speed and opportunistic matchups at the top and bottom of the order. **Henry Bolte** earns a 61.01 score, driven largely by his leadoff status and a 10% park factor boost against Matthews. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (60.01) is cleared for action due to a substantial 14% platoon edge against Cavalli. The most difficult decision of the morning was sitting **Zach McKinstry**, who finished at 38.26. While he had moderate park advantages, the SP skill of Rasmussen proved too suppressive, keeping him strictly below our 40-point floor for activation.\n\nManagers should remain wary of the 48.34 score assigned to **Josh Naylor**. While he is currently slotted in, he is facing Wheeler, an elite arm with a 3.06 xERA, and the negative park and pitcher skill factors suggest a high floor of variance. We are effectively betting on his talent to outweigh the environmental friction. Our bench remains depleted with **James Wood** still on the IL and **Jose Caballero** unavailable due to the team\u2019s off-day, meaning our focus remains entirely on the high-upside speed threats currently in the starting seven.",
